Good news on the Sentieon front!

1) All of the intermediate files which are currently deleted have a flag setting which will retain them.   BTW- the short reads produce 1 cram , and the long reads a secondlong read cram.  VCF entries contain annotations informing you how many reads of each caller type support the call . PLEASE CONSULT DOCS ON APPROPRIOATE FLAGS TO KEEP TEMP FILES AND DIRS AND TO EMIT ALL THREE VCF types.

2) There are three vcfs sentieon can emit: snv.vcf (variants 0 to 50bp), sv.vcf(variants of 51 to 10K'ish bp) and cnv.vcf (10K'ish bp and above).  The cnv.vcf was NOT being emitted properly, and I have the fix for this.

3) Special callers:  I have the command invocation for the pre-releaser SegDup Sentieon caller (which includes SMN, PMS2, etc).  https://github.com/Sentieon/segdup-caller

4) Mito calling. I was provided the pre-release version of this caller and will run it.  bin/sentieon_mitochondrial_pipeline.sh
